// TASK-178. The board rendered this `notes` button on every row - all 69 visible ones, byte for
// byte - while only 12 of the owner's 83 jobs carried a general note, so it announced a note where
// there was nothing behind it and meant nothing anywhere. It now renders only when the list
// response's `note_preview` is non-empty; hover or focus shows that first line, and the click still
// opens the same read/edit modal (openNoteModal), which is the only place a note is written.
// Consequence worth knowing: a job with no note no longer offers one-click note creation from the
// board. Its `details` link still reaches JobNotes on the job page, which is where a first note gets
// written - the owner chose an indicator that means something over a button on every row.
// The preview is portalled to <body> as `fixed` for TASK-173's reason, not for tidiness: the desktop
